---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How often should I measure my bra size?",
    answer: "We recommend measuring every 6 months, or whenever you experience changes in body weight, workout routines, or life events. Follow our step-by-step <a href='/#how-to-measure' class='text-primary font-medium hover:underline'>measurement guide</a> to keep your numbers up to date!"
  },
  {
    question: "What if my calculated size is different from what I currently wear?",
    answer: "It is very common to wear a size different from your calculated size without realizing it, as sizing matrices can differ between manufacturers. Our <a href='/#calculator' class='text-primary font-medium hover:underline'>bra size calculator</a> provides a dependable starting baseline based on current standards."
  },
  {
    question: "What are 'Sister Sizes' and how do I use them?",
    answer: "Sister sizes share the same cup volume but have different band sizes. For example, 34C, 32D, and 36B hold equivalent cup volumes. Use our interactive <a href='/#calculator' class='text-primary font-medium hover:underline'>sister size comparison</a> to see your exact sister sizes."
  },
  {
    question: "Should I wear a bra when measuring?",
    answer: "Yes, measure while wearing an unlined, non-padded, lightly supported bra. Avoid padded or push-up bras as they add artificial bulk, and check our <a href='/#how-to-measure' class='text-primary font-medium hover:underline'>how to measure instructions</a>."
  },
  {
    question: "How should a well-fitting bra actually feel?",
    answer: "The band should sit level across your back without riding up or digging in (providing the majority of the bra's support). Refer to our <a href='/#fit-guide' class='text-primary font-medium hover:underline'>fit diagnostic guide</a> if you experience band or strap slipping."
  },
  {
    question: "Why do bra sizes vary between different brands?",
    answer: "Different manufacturers use varying sizing matrices, fabric elasticity, and wire shapes. Use your calculated size as a primary starting point and refer to our <a href='/#chart-section' class='text-primary font-medium hover:underline'>international size converter chart</a> when buying."
  }
];
---

<section id="faq" class="py-10 sm:py-16 md:py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="mb-8 sm:mb-12 text-center md:text-left">
    <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
      FAQ
    </span>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-lg text-body max-w-2xl">
      Everything you need to know about measuring, bra sizing, and finding your most comfortable fit.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <details class="group bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4 sm:p-6 cursor-pointer hover:border-hairline-strong transition-all duration-200 shadow-xs">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-base md:text-lg text-ink list-none">
          <span class="pr-2">{faq.question}</span>
          <span class="transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-primary flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-4 text-body text-sm md:text-base pt-4 border-t border-hairline leading-relaxed">
          <p set:html={faq.answer} />
        </div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
